  ('money-basics-101', 'example', '{"text": "Example: time value of money\n\nYour savings account gives 2% interest while inflation is 3%. What is your real return?\n\nThis illustrates how time value of money applies in a real Indonesian financial context. Understanding this scenario helps learners recognize similar situations in their own financial decisions.", "source_ids": ["ad0e8258-4e0a-4378-b257-4fd3628c6953", "7f4b83f2-8f1d-415c-9d4f-64e6284bef04"]}'::jsonb, 'intermediate', 'money_basics', true, '2026-07-14T14:21:14.795171'::timestamptz),
  ('money-basics-101', 'example', '{"text": "Example: compound interest basics\n\nYou must choose between buying a laptop now or waiting 6 months for a 15% discount. What factors matter?\n\nThis illustrates how compound interest basics applies in a real Indonesian financial context. Understanding this scenario helps learners recognize similar situations in their own financial decisions.", "source_ids": ["ad0e8258-4e0a-4378-b257-4fd3628c6953", "7f4b83f2-8f1d-415c-9d4f-64e6284bef04"]}'::jsonb, 'intermediate', 'money_basics', true, '2026-07-14T14:21:14.795177'::timestamptz),
  ('money-basics-101', 'example', '{"text": "Example: inflation impact on savings\n\nA fintech app offers 8% on deposits but is not OJK-licensed. A bank offers 4% with OJK license. Compare risks.\n\nThis illustrates how inflation impact on savings applies in a real Indonesian financial context. Understanding this scenario helps learners recognize similar situations in their own financial decisions.", "source_ids": ["ad0e8258-4e0a-4378-b257-4fd3628c6953", "7f4b83f2-8f1d-415c-9d4f-64e6284bef04"]}'::jsonb, 'intermediate', 'money_basics', true, '2026-07-14T14:21:14.795183'::timestamptz),
  ('money-basics-101', 'example', '{"text": "Example: bank vs fintech\n\nYou want to save for a Rp 50M motorcycle in 3 years. How much must you save monthly at 5% annual return?\n\nThis illustrates how bank vs fintech applies in a real Indonesian financial context. Understanding this scenario helps learners recognize similar situations in their own financial decisions.", "source_ids": ["ad0e8258-4e0a-4378-b257-4fd3628c6953", "7f4b83f2-8f1d-415c-9d4f-64e6284bef04"]}'::jsonb, 'intermediate', 'money_basics', true, '2026-07-14T14:21:14.795188'::timestamptz),
  ('money-basics-101', 'example', '{"text": "Example: behavioral biases in spending\n\nAn unlicensed P2P lender uses ''social proof'' from fake testimonials. Design a consumer protection framework.\n\nThis illustrates how behavioral biases in spending applies in a real Indonesian financial context. Understanding this scenario helps learners recognize similar situations in their own financial decisions.", "source_ids": ["ad0e8258-4e0a-4378-b257-4fd3628c6953", "7f4b83f2-8f1d-415c-9d4f-64e6284bef04"]}'::jsonb, 'advanced', 'money_basics', true, '2026-07-14T14:21:14.795198'::timestamptz),
  ('money-basics-101', 'example', '{"text": "Example: mental accounting\n\nA fintech gamifies spending with cashback rewards. Users overspend by 30%. Analyze the behavioral mechanism.\n\nThis illustrates how mental accounting applies in a real Indonesian financial context. Understanding this scenario helps learners recognize similar situations in their own financial decisions.", "source_ids": ["ad0e8258-4e0a-4378-b257-4fd3628c6953", "7f4b83f2-8f1d-415c-9d4f-64e6284bef04"]}'::jsonb, 'advanced', 'money_basics', true, '2026-07-14T14:21:14.795206'::timestamptz),
  ('money-basics-101', 'example', '{"text": "Example: anchoring in pricing\n\nCompare the effective cost of ''pay later'' schemes (0% interest, 2% admin fee) vs credit cards (2% monthly).\n\nThis illustrates how anchoring in pricing applies in a real Indonesian financial context. Understanding this scenario helps learners recognize similar situations in their own financial decisions.", "source_ids": ["ad0e8258-4e0a-4378-b257-4fd3628c6953", "7f4b83f2-8f1d-415c-9d4f-64e6284bef04"]}'::jsonb, 'advanced', 'money_basics', true, '2026-07-14T14:21:14.795212'::timestamptz),
  ('money-basics-101', 'example', '{"text": "Example: present bias\n\nA new e-wallet offers 10% cashback for the first month. Model the customer acquisition cost and churn risk.\n\nThis illustrates how present bias applies in a real Indonesian financial context. Understanding this scenario helps learners recognize similar situations in their own financial decisions.", "source_ids": ["ad0e8258-4e0a-4378-b257-4fd3628c6953", "7f4b83f2-8f1d-415c-9d4f-64e6284bef04"]}'::jsonb, 'advanced', 'money_basics', true, '2026-07-14T14:21:14.795218'::timestamptz),
  ('money-basics-101', 'example', '{"text": "Example: hyperbolic discounting\n\nDesign a financial literacy intervention for rural Indonesia using behavioral nudging principles.\n\nThis illustrates how hyperbolic discounting applies in a real Indonesian financial context. Understanding this scenario helps learners recognize similar situations in their own financial decisions.", "source_ids": ["ad0e8258-4e0a-4378-b257-4fd3628c6953", "7f4b83f2-8f1d-415c-9d4f-64e6284bef04"]}'::jsonb, 'advanced', 'money_basics', true, '2026-07-14T14:21:14.795223'::timestamptz),
  ('inflation-101', 'example', '{"text": "Example: price increases\n\nA bowl of noodles cost Rp 15,000 last year and Rp 16,500 now. What is the inflation rate?\n\nThis illustrates how price increases applies in a real Indonesian financial context. Understanding this scenario helps learners recognize similar situations in their own financial decisions.", "source_ids": ["e49fe239-c534-4bed-b0bd-a7950b9e35c4", "097b62c4-9aae-4933-a870-ac74a526b8f1"]}'::jsonb, 'beginner', 'inflation', true, '2026-07-14T14:21:14.795229'::timestamptz),
  ('inflation-101', 'example', '{"text": "Example: purchasing power\n\nYour parents say they bought a house for Rp 50M in 2000. What would it cost today with 5% average inflation?\n\nThis illustrates how purchasing power applies in a real Indonesian financial context. Understanding this scenario helps learners recognize similar situations in their own financial decisions.", "source_ids": ["e49fe239-c534-4bed-b0bd-a7950b9e35c4", "097b62c4-9aae-4933-a870-ac74a526b8f1"]}'::jsonb, 'beginner', 'inflation', true, '2026-07-14T14:21:14.795236'::timestamptz),
  ('inflation-101', 'example', '{"text": "Example: BI inflation target\n\nBank Indonesia targets 2.5% inflation. Why is some inflation considered healthy?\n\nThis illustrates how BI inflation target applies in a real Indonesian financial context. Understanding this scenario helps learners recognize similar situations in their own financial decisions.", "source_ids": ["e49fe239-c534-4bed-b0bd-a7950b9e35c4", "097b62c4-9aae-4933-a870-ac74a526b8f1"]}'::jsonb, 'beginner', 'inflation', true, '2026-07-14T14:21:14.795242'::timestamptz),
  ('inflation-101', 'example', '{"text": "Example: CPI basics\n\nIf your savings earn 3% but inflation is 4%, are you getting richer or poorer?\n\nThis illustrates how CPI basics applies in a real Indonesian financial context. Understanding this scenario helps learners recognize similar situations in their own financial decisions.", "source_ids": ["e49fe239-c534-4bed-b0bd-a7950b9e35c4", "097b62c4-9aae-4933-a870-ac74a526b8f1"]}'::jsonb, 'beginner', 'inflation', true, '2026-07-14T14:21:14.795249'::timestamptz),
  ('inflation-101', 'example', '{"text": "Example: inflation vs deflation\n\nA store raises prices by 10% during Ramadan. Is this inflation or something else?\n\nThis illustrates how inflation vs deflation applies in a real Indonesian financial context. Understanding this scenario helps learners recognize similar situations in their own financial decisions.", "source_ids": ["e49fe239-c534-4bed-b0bd-a7950b9e35c4", "097b62c4-9aae-4933-a870-ac74a526b8f1"]}'::jsonb, 'beginner', 'inflation', true, '2026-07-14T14:21:14.795254'::timestamptz),
  ('inflation-101', 'example', '{"text": "Example: real vs nominal interest rates\n\nThe BI rate is 5.75%, inflation is 2.8%. Calculate the approximate real interest rate.\n\nThis illustrates how real vs nominal interest rates applies in a real Indonesian financial context. Understanding this scenario helps learners recognize similar situations in their own financial decisions.", "source_ids": ["e49fe239-c534-4bed-b0bd-a7950b9e35c4", "097b62c4-9aae-4933-a870-ac74a526b8f1"]}'::jsonb, 'intermediate', 'inflation', true, '2026-07-14T14:21:14.795260'::timestamptz),
  ('inflation-101', 'example', '{"text": "Example: inflation-indexed bonds\n\nIndonesia imports 30% of its consumer goods. The Rupiah depreciates 10%. Estimate the inflation impact.\n\nThis illustrates how inflation-indexed bonds applies in a real Indonesian financial context. Understanding this scenario helps learners recognize similar situations in their own financial decisions.", "source_ids": ["e49fe239-c534-4bed-b0bd-a7950b9e35c4", "097b62c4-9aae-4933-a870-ac74a526b8f1"]}'::jsonb, 'intermediate', 'inflation', true, '2026-07-14T14:21:14.795265'::timestamptz),
  ('inflation-101', 'example', '{"text": "Example: Fisher equation\n\nCompare cost-push inflation (oil price shock) vs demand-pull inflation (fiscal stimulus). Which is harder to control?\n\nThis illustrates how Fisher equation applies in a real Indonesian financial context. Understanding this scenario helps learners recognize similar situations in their own financial decisions.", "source_ids": ["e49fe239-c534-4bed-b0bd-a7950b9e35c4", "097b62c4-9aae-4933-a870-ac74a526b8f1"]}'::jsonb, 'intermediate', 'inflation', true, '2026-07-14T14:21:14.795271'::timestamptz),
  ('inflation-101', 'example', '{"text": "Example: cost-push vs demand-pull inflation\n\nA company gives 8% raises when inflation is 3%. What happens to their competitiveness vs foreign rivals?\n\nThis illustrates how cost-push vs demand-pull inflation applies in a real Indonesian financial context. Understanding this scenario helps learners recognize similar situations in their own financial decisions.", "source_ids": ["e49fe239-c534-4bed-b0bd-a7950b9e35c4", "097b62c4-9aae-4933-a870-ac74a526b8f1"]}'::jsonb, 'intermediate', 'inflation', true, '2026-07-14T14:21:14.795277'::timestamptz),
  ('inflation-101', 'example', '{"text": "Example: monetary policy transmission\n\nGovernment raises fuel subsidies. How does this affect reported inflation vs actual cost of living?\n\nThis illustrates how monetary policy transmission applies in a real Indonesian financial context. Understanding this scenario helps learners recognize similar situations in their own financial decisions.", "source_ids": ["e49fe239-c534-4bed-b0bd-a7950b9e35c4", "097b62c4-9aae-4933-a870-ac74a526b8f1"]}'::jsonb, 'intermediate', 'inflation', true, '2026-07-14T14:21:14.795282'::timestamptz),
  ('inflation-101', 'example', '{"text": "Example: Phillips curve\n\nIndonesia''s debt-to-GDP is 41%. If BI monetizes 10% of new issuance, model the inflation risk over 5 years.\n\nThis illustrates how Phillips curve applies in a real Indonesian financial context. Understanding this scenario helps learners recognize similar situations in their own financial decisions.", "source_ids": ["e49fe239-c534-4bed-b0bd-a7950b9e35c4", "097b62c4-9aae-4933-a870-ac74a526b8f1"]}'::jsonb, 'advanced', 'inflation', true, '2026-07-14T14:21:14.795288'::timestamptz),
  ('inflation-101', 'example', '{"text": "Example: Taylor rule\n\nDesign an inflation swap hedging strategy for a pension fund with Rp 500B in fixed-income assets.\n\nThis illustrates how Taylor rule applies in a real Indonesian financial context. Understanding this scenario helps learners recognize similar situations in their own financial decisions.", "source_ids": ["e49fe239-c534-4bed-b0bd-a7950b9e35c4", "097b62c4-9aae-4933-a870-ac74a526b8f1"]}'::jsonb, 'advanced', 'inflation', true, '2026-07-14T14:21:14.795293'::timestamptz),
  ('inflation-101', 'example', '{"text": "Example: quantitative easing effects\n\nCompare BI''s inflation targeting framework (2016-present) with the pre-2016 multiple-indicator approach.\n\nThis illustrates how quantitative easing effects applies in a real Indonesian financial context. Understanding this scenario helps learners recognize similar situations in their own financial decisions.", "source_ids": ["e49fe239-c534-4bed-b0bd-a7950b9e35c4", "097b62c4-9aae-4933-a870-ac74a526b8f1"]}'::jsonb, 'advanced', 'inflation', true, '2026-07-14T14:21:14.795299'::timestamptz),
  ('inflation-101', 'example', '{"text": "Example: inflation targeting framework\n\nA commodity exporter faces terms-of-trade shock. Should BI prioritize inflation target or growth?\n\nThis illustrates how inflation targeting framework applies in a real Indonesian financial context. Understanding this scenario helps learners recognize similar situations in their own financial decisions.", "source_ids": ["e49fe239-c534-4bed-b0bd-a7950b9e35c4", "097b62c4-9aae-4933-a870-ac74a526b8f1"]}'::jsonb, 'advanced', 'inflation', true, '2026-07-14T14:21:14.795305'::timestamptz),
  ('inflation-101', 'example', '{"text": "Example: financial repression\n\nModel the pass-through of a 20% minimum wage increase to CPI, assuming 40% labor share in production.\n\nThis illustrates how financial repression applies in a real Indonesian financial context. Understanding this scenario helps learners recognize similar situations in their own financial decisions.", "source_ids": ["e49fe239-c534-4bed-b0bd-a7950b9e35c4", "097b62c4-9aae-4933-a870-ac74a526b8f1"]}'::jsonb, 'advanced', 'inflation', true, '2026-07-14T14:21:14.795310'::timestamptz),
  ('budgeting-101', 'example', '{"text": "Example: 50/30/20 rule\n\nYou earn Rp 5M/month. Apply the 50/30/20 rule. How much for needs, wants, and savings?\n\nThis illustrates how 50/30/20 rule applies in a real Indonesian financial context. Understanding this scenario helps learners recognize similar situations in their own financial decisions.", "source_ids": ["7f4b83f2-8f1d-415c-9d4f-64e6284bef04", "f7003b72-8158-4a9e-a853-1c3bf914ea4a"]}'::jsonb, 'beginner', 'budgeting', true, '2026-07-14T14:21:14.795316'::timestamptz),
  ('budgeting-101', 'example', '{"text": "Example: tracking expenses\n\nYou always run out of money by the 20th. What budgeting habit should you start first?\n\nThis illustrates how tracking expenses applies in a real Indonesian financial context. Understanding this scenario helps learners recognize similar situations in their own financial decisions.", "source_ids": ["7f4b83f2-8f1d-415c-9d4f-64e6284bef04", "f7003b72-8158-4a9e-a853-1c3bf914ea4a"]}'::jsonb, 'beginner', 'budgeting', true, '2026-07-14T14:21:14.795322'::timestamptz),
  ('budgeting-101', 'example', '{"text": "Example: saving first\n\nYour friend uses 6 different e-wallets and loses track of spending. What is a simple fix?\n\nThis illustrates how saving first applies in a real Indonesian financial context. Understanding this scenario helps learners recognize similar situations in their own financial decisions.", "source_ids": ["7f4b83f2-8f1d-415c-9d4f-64e6284bef04", "f7003b72-8158-4a9e-a853-1c3bf914ea4a"]}'::jsonb, 'beginner', 'budgeting', true, '2026-07-14T14:21:14.795327'::timestamptz),
  ('budgeting-101', 'example', '{"text": "Example: envelope method\n\nYou want to build a 3-month emergency fund earning Rp 4M/month. How much do you need?\n\nThis illustrates how envelope method applies in a real Indonesian financial context. Understanding this scenario helps learners recognize similar situations in their own financial decisions.", "source_ids": ["7f4b83f2-8f1d-415c-9d4f-64e6284bef04", "f7003b72-8158-4a9e-a853-1c3bf914ea4a"]}'::jsonb, 'beginner', 'budgeting', true, '2026-07-14T14:21:14.795333'::timestamptz),
  ('budgeting-101', 'example', '{"text": "Example: needs vs wants budget\n\nYou spend Rp 2M/month on food delivery. What is one way to cut this without cooking every day?\n\nThis illustrates how needs vs wants budget applies in a real Indonesian financial context. Understanding this scenario helps learners recognize similar situations in their own financial decisions.", "source_ids": ["7f4b83f2-8f1d-415c-9d4f-64e6284bef04", "f7003b72-8158-4a9e-a853-1c3bf914ea4a"]}'::jsonb, 'beginner', 'budgeting', true, '2026-07-14T14:21:14.795338'::timestamptz),
  ('budgeting-101', 'example', '{"text": "Example: zero-based budgeting\n\nYou have Rp 3M in credit card debt at 2.5%/month and Rp 5M in student loans at 0.8%/month. Which to pay first?\n\nThis illustrates how zero-based budgeting applies in a real Indonesian financial context. Understanding this scenario helps learners recognize similar situations in their own financial decisions.", "source_ids": ["7f4b83f2-8f1d-415c-9d4f-64e6284bef04", "f7003b72-8158-4a9e-a853-1c3bf914ea4a"]}'::jsonb, 'intermediate', 'budgeting', true, '2026-07-14T14:21:14.795344'::timestamptz),
  ('budgeting-101', 'example', '{"text": "Example: pay yourself first\n\nCreate a 12-month cash flow forecast for a freelancer with irregular income (Rp 3M–8M/month).\n\nThis illustrates how pay yourself first applies in a real Indonesian financial context. Understanding this scenario helps learners recognize similar situations in their own financial decisions.", "source_ids": ["7f4b83f2-8f1d-415c-9d4f-64e6284bef04", "f7003b72-8158-4a9e-a853-1c3bf914ea4a"]}'::jsonb, 'intermediate', 'budgeting', true, '2026-07-14T14:21:14.795351'::timestamptz),
  ('budgeting-101', 'example', '{"text": "Example: sinking funds\n\nYou want to buy a Rp 300M house in 5 years. You have Rp 50M saved. Model monthly savings needed at 6% return.\n\nThis illustrates how sinking funds applies in a real Indonesian financial context. Understanding this scenario helps learners recognize similar situations in their own financial decisions.", "source_ids": ["7f4b83f2-8f1d-415c-9d4f-64e6284bef04", "f7003b72-8158-4a9e-a853-1c3bf914ea4a"]}'::jsonb, 'intermediate', 'budgeting', true, '2026-07-14T14:21:14.795356'::timestamptz),
  ('budgeting-101', 'example', '{"text": "Example: debt snowball vs avalanche\n\nYour actual spending is 15% higher than budgeted in 3 categories. How do you diagnose and fix?\n\nThis illustrates how debt snowball vs avalanche applies in a real Indonesian financial context. Understanding this scenario helps learners recognize similar situations in their own financial decisions.", "source_ids": ["7f4b83f2-8f1d-415c-9d4f-64e6284bef04", "f7003b72-8158-4a9e-a853-1c3bf914ea4a"]}'::jsonb, 'intermediate', 'budgeting', true, '2026-07-14T14:21:14.795362'::timestamptz),
  ('budgeting-101', 'example', '{"text": "Example: opportunity cost of spending\n\nCompare zero-based budgeting (start from zero each month) vs incremental budgeting (last month + X%).\n\nThis illustrates how opportunity cost of spending applies in a real Indonesian financial context. Understanding this scenario helps learners recognize similar situations in their own financial decisions.", "source_ids": ["7f4b83f2-8f1d-415c-9d4f-64e6284bef04", "f7003b72-8158-4a9e-a853-1c3bf914ea4a"]}'::jsonb, 'intermediate', 'budgeting', true, '2026-07-14T14:21:14.795367'::timestamptz),
  ('budgeting-101', 'example', '{"text": "Example: capital budgeting\n\nA 30-year-old professional must choose: MBA (Rp 500M cost, +30% salary) vs invest in property. Model NPV.\n\nThis illustrates how capital budgeting applies in a real Indonesian financial context. Understanding this scenario helps learners recognize similar situations in their own financial decisions.", "source_ids": ["7f4b83f2-8f1d-415c-9d4f-64e6284bef04", "f7003b72-8158-4a9e-a853-1c3bf914ea4a"]}'::jsonb, 'advanced', 'budgeting', true, '2026-07-14T14:21:14.795373'::timestamptz),
  ('budgeting-101', 'example', '{"text": "Example: NPV vs IRR in personal finance\n\nUsing lifecycle hypothesis, how should a person''s savings rate change from age 25 to 60 in Indonesia?\n\nThis illustrates how NPV vs IRR in personal finance applies in a real Indonesian financial context. Understanding this scenario helps learners recognize similar situations in their own financial decisions.", "source_ids": ["7f4b83f2-8f1d-415c-9d4f-64e6284bef04", "f7003b72-8158-4a9e-a853-1c3bf914ea4a"]}'::jsonb, 'advanced', 'budgeting', true, '2026-07-14T14:21:14.795379'::timestamptz),
  ('budgeting-101', 'example', '{"text": "Example: lifecycle hypothesis\n\nDesign a stochastic budgeting model for a dual-income family with one partner in gig economy.\n\nThis illustrates how lifecycle hypothesis applies in a real Indonesian financial context. Understanding this scenario helps learners recognize similar situations in their own financial decisions.", "source_ids": ["7f4b83f2-8f1d-415c-9d4f-64e6284bef04", "f7003b72-8158-4a9e-a853-1c3bf914ea4a"]}'::jsonb, 'advanced', 'budgeting', true, '2026-07-14T14:21:14.795384'::timestamptz),
  ('budgeting-101', 'example', '{"text": "Example: permanent income hypothesis\n\nCompare consumption smoothing via insurance vs self-insurance for a family with Rp 200M annual income.\n\nThis illustrates how permanent income hypothesis applies in a real Indonesian financial context. Understanding this scenario helps learners recognize similar situations in their own financial decisions.", "source_ids": ["7f4b83f2-8f1d-415c-9d4f-64e6284bef04", "f7003b72-8158-4a9e-a853-1c3bf914ea4a"]}'::jsonb, 'advanced', 'budgeting', true, '2026-07-14T14:21:14.795390'::timestamptz),
  ('budgeting-101', 'example', '{"text": "Example: stochastic budgeting\n\nA parent considers leaving Rp 1B inheritance vs spending it on children''s education. Model the trade-off.\n\nThis illustrates how stochastic budgeting applies in a real Indonesian financial context. Understanding this scenario helps learners recognize similar situations in their own financial decisions.", "source_ids": ["7f4b83f2-8f1d-415c-9d4f-64e6284bef04", "f7003b72-8158-4a9e-a853-1c3bf914ea4a"]}'::jsonb, 'advanced', 'budgeting', true, '2026-07-14T14:21:14.795395'::timestamptz),
  ('risk-return-101', 'example', '{"text": "Example: risk vs reward\n\nYou have Rp 10M. Bank deposit gives 4%, stock market averages 10% historically. Compare after 10 years.\n\nThis illustrates how risk vs reward applies in a real Indonesian financial context. Understanding this scenario helps learners recognize similar situations in their own financial decisions.", "source_ids": ["f7003b72-8158-4a9e-a853-1c3bf914ea4a", "eca56a9e-df9b-432f-b360-c1ab6450a2ae"]}'::jsonb, 'beginner', 'risk_return', true, '2026-07-14T14:21:14.795401'::timestamptz),
  ('risk-return-101', 'example', '{"text": "Example: compound interest magic\n\nYour friend made 50% in crypto last month. Should you invest all your savings there?\n\nThis illustrates how compound interest magic applies in a real Indonesian financial context. Understanding this scenario helps learners recognize similar situations in their own financial decisions.", "source_ids": ["f7003b72-8158-4a9e-a853-1c3bf914ea4a", "eca56a9e-df9b-432f-b360-c1ab6450a2ae"]}'::jsonb, 'beginner', 'risk_return', true, '2026-07-14T14:21:14.795407'::timestamptz),
  ('risk-return-101', 'example', '{"text": "Example: time in market\n\nUsing the Rule of 72, how long does it take to double money at 6% annual return?\n\nThis illustrates how time in market applies in a real Indonesian financial context. Understanding this scenario helps learners recognize similar situations in their own financial decisions.", "source_ids": ["f7003b72-8158-4a9e-a853-1c3bf914ea4a", "eca56a9e-df9b-432f-b360-c1ab6450a2ae"]}'::jsonb, 'beginner', 'risk_return', true, '2026-07-14T14:21:14.795412'::timestamptz),
  ('risk-return-101', 'example', '{"text": "Example: diversification basics\n\nA bond pays 6% fixed. A stock might return 15% or lose 10%. Which is riskier?\n\nThis illustrates how diversification basics applies in a real Indonesian financial context. Understanding this scenario helps learners recognize similar situations in their own financial decisions.", "source_ids": ["f7003b72-8158-4a9e-a853-1c3bf914ea4a", "eca56a9e-df9b-432f-b360-c1ab6450a2ae"]}'::jsonb, 'beginner', 'risk_return', true, '2026-07-14T14:21:14.795418'::timestamptz),
  ('risk-return-101', 'example', '{"text": "Example: not putting eggs in one basket\n\nYou split Rp 20M equally across 5 stocks vs putting all in 1 stock. Which is safer?\n\nThis illustrates how not putting eggs in one basket applies in a real Indonesian financial context. Understanding this scenario helps learners recognize similar situations in their own financial decisions.", "source_ids": ["f7003b72-8158-4a9e-a853-1c3bf914ea4a", "eca56a9e-df9b-432f-b360-c1ab6450a2ae"]}'::jsonb, 'beginner', 'risk_return', true, '2026-07-14T14:21:14.795423'::timestamptz),
  ('risk-return-101', 'example', '{"text": "Example: Sharpe ratio\n\nPortfolio A: 8% return, 12% volatility. Portfolio B: 10% return, 20% volatility. Risk-free rate is 5%. Which has better Sharpe ratio?\n\nThis illustrates how Sharpe ratio applies in a real Indonesian financial context. Understanding this scenario helps learners recognize similar situations in their own financial decisions.", "source_ids": ["f7003b72-8158-4a9e-a853-1c3bf914ea4a", "eca56a9e-df9b-432f-b360-c1ab6450a2ae"]}'::jsonb, 'intermediate', 'risk_return', true, '2026-07-14T14:21:14.795429'::timestamptz),
  ('risk-return-101', 'example', '{"text": "Example: standard deviation\n\nA stock has beta 1.5. The market goes up 10%. What is the expected stock return?\n\nThis illustrates how standard deviation applies in a real Indonesian financial context. Understanding this scenario helps learners recognize similar situations in their own financial decisions.", "source_ids": ["f7003b72-8158-4a9e-a853-1c3bf914ea4a", "eca56a9e-df9b-432f-b360-c1ab6450a2ae"]}'::jsonb, 'intermediate', 'risk_return', true, '2026-07-14T14:21:14.795434'::timestamptz),
  ('risk-return-101', 'example', '{"text": "Example: beta\n\nYou invest Rp 2M monthly (DCA) vs Rp 24M lump sum. Under what market conditions does each win?\n\nThis illustrates how beta applies in a real Indonesian financial context. Understanding this scenario helps learners recognize similar situations in their own financial decisions.", "source_ids": ["f7003b72-8158-4a9e-a853-1c3bf914ea4a", "eca56a9e-df9b-432f-b360-c1ab6450a2ae"]}'::jsonb, 'intermediate', 'risk_return', true, '2026-07-14T14:21:14.795440'::timestamptz),
  ('risk-return-101', 'example', '{"text": "Example: alpha\n\nYour portfolio is 70% stocks, 30% bonds. After a bull run, it''s 85% stocks. Should you rebalance?\n\nThis illustrates how alpha applies in a real Indonesian financial context. Understanding this scenario helps learners recognize similar situations in their own financial decisions.", "source_ids": ["f7003b72-8158-4a9e-a853-1c3bf914ea4a", "eca56a9e-df9b-432f-b360-c1ab6450a2ae"]}'::jsonb, 'intermediate', 'risk_return', true, '2026-07-14T14:21:14.795446'::timestamptz),
  ('risk-return-101', 'example', '{"text": "Example: systematic vs unsystematic risk\n\nCalculate the expected return of a portfolio: 40% BBCA (beta 0.9), 30% BBRI (beta 1.1), 30% bonds (beta 0).\n\nThis illustrates how systematic vs unsystematic risk applies in a real Indonesian financial context. Understanding this scenario helps learners recognize similar situations in their own financial decisions.", "source_ids": ["f7003b72-8158-4a9e-a853-1c3bf914ea4a", "eca56a9e-df9b-432f-b360-c1ab6450a2ae"]}'::jsonb, 'intermediate', 'risk_return', true, '2026-07-14T14:21:14.795452'::timestamptz),
  ('risk-return-101', 'example', '{"text": "Example: Black-Scholes intuition\n\nA fund has daily returns with mean 0.05% and std dev 1.2%. Calculate 95% 1-day VaR for Rp 1B portfolio.\n\nThis illustrates how Black-Scholes intuition applies in a real Indonesian financial context. Understanding this scenario helps learners recognize similar situations in their own financial decisions.", "source_ids": ["f7003b72-8158-4a9e-a853-1c3bf914ea4a", "eca56a9e-df9b-432f-b360-c1ab6450a2ae"]}'::jsonb, 'advanced', 'risk_return', true, '2026-07-14T14:21:14.795458'::timestamptz),
  ('risk-return-101', 'example', '{"text": "Example: Value at Risk (VaR)\n\nCompare Sortino ratio vs Sharpe ratio for a hedge fund with frequent small gains and rare large losses.\n\nThis illustrates how Value at Risk (VaR) applies in a real Indonesian financial context. Understanding this scenario helps learners recognize similar situations in their own financial decisions.", "source_ids": ["f7003b72-8158-4a9e-a853-1c3bf914ea4a", "eca56a9e-df9b-432f-b360-c1ab6450a2ae"]}'::jsonb, 'advanced', 'risk_return', true, '2026-07-14T14:21:14.795463'::timestamptz),
  ('risk-return-101', 'example', '{"text": "Example: Conditional VaR\n\nDesign a minimum-variance portfolio using Indonesian stocks (BBCA, BBRI, TLKM, UNVR, ASII) with covariance matrix.\n\nThis illustrates how Conditional VaR applies in a real Indonesian financial context. Understanding this scenario helps learners recognize similar situations in their own financial decisions.", "source_ids": ["f7003b72-8158-4a9e-a853-1c3bf914ea4a", "eca56a9e-df9b-432f-b360-c1ab6450a2ae"]}'::jsonb, 'advanced', 'risk_return', true, '2026-07-14T14:21:14.795469'::timestamptz),
  ('risk-return-101', 'example', '{"text": "Example: drawdown analysis\n\nA momentum factor strategy in IDX has 15% annual return but 30% max drawdown. Is this acceptable for a pension fund?\n\nThis illustrates how drawdown analysis applies in a real Indonesian financial context. Understanding this scenario helps learners recognize similar situations in their own financial decisions.", "source_ids": ["f7003b72-8158-4a9e-a853-1c3bf914ea4a", "eca56a9e-df9b-432f-b360-c1ab6450a2ae"]}'::jsonb, 'advanced', 'risk_return', true, '2026-07-14T14:21:14.795474'::timestamptz),
  ('risk-return-101', 'example', '{"text": "Example: maximum drawdown\n\nExplain why the efficient frontier shifts when adding Indonesian government bonds (SUN) to an all-equity portfolio.\n\nThis illustrates how maximum drawdown applies in a real Indonesian financial context. Understanding this scenario helps learners recognize similar situations in their own financial decisions.", "source_ids": ["f7003b72-8158-4a9e-a853-1c3bf914ea4a", "eca56a9e-df9b-432f-b360-c1ab6450a2ae"]}'::jsonb, 'advanced', 'risk_return', true, '2026-07-14T14:21:14.795480'::timestamptz),
  ('idx-basics-101', 'example', '{"text": "Example: what is IDX\n\nYou buy 100 shares of BBCA at Rp 8,000. The price rises to Rp 9,000. What is your profit?\n\nThis illustrates how what is IDX applies in a real Indonesian financial context. Understanding this scenario helps learners recognize similar situations in their own financial decisions.", "source_ids": ["c7c57d03-733f-4fe8-bd15-ce3a1cd4a760", "58e3fb2d-7dbc-4a08-ab1a-379af3fa5c38"]}'::jsonb, 'beginner', 'idx_basics', true, '2026-07-14T14:21:14.795485'::timestamptz),
  ('idx-basics-101', 'example', '{"text": "Example: stock vs company\n\nWhat is the difference between owning 100 shares of a company and working for that company?\n\nThis illustrates how stock vs company applies in a real Indonesian financial context. Understanding this scenario helps learners recognize similar situations in their own financial decisions.", "source_ids": ["c7c57d03-733f-4fe8-bd15-ce3a1cd4a760", "58e3fb2d-7dbc-4a08-ab1a-379af3fa5c38"]}'::jsonb, 'beginner', 'idx_basics', true, '2026-07-14T14:21:14.795491'::timestamptz),
  ('idx-basics-101', 'example', '{"text": "Example: buying shares\n\nIDX opens at 9 AM and closes at 4 PM. Can you place orders at 8:30 AM?\n\nThis illustrates how buying shares applies in a real Indonesian financial context. Understanding this scenario helps learners recognize similar situations in their own financial decisions.", "source_ids": ["c7c57d03-733f-4fe8-bd15-ce3a1cd4a760", "58e3fb2d-7dbc-4a08-ab1a-379af3fa5c38"]}'::jsonb, 'beginner', 'idx_basics', true, '2026-07-14T14:21:14.795496'::timestamptz),
  ('idx-basics-101', 'example', '{"text": "Example: stock price basics\n\nA company announces a 2:1 stock split. You own 50 shares at Rp 10,000. What happens?\n\nThis illustrates how stock price basics applies in a real Indonesian financial context. Understanding this scenario helps learners recognize similar situations in their own financial decisions.", "source_ids": ["c7c57d03-733f-4fe8-bd15-ce3a1cd4a760", "58e3fb2d-7dbc-4a08-ab1a-379af3fa5c38"]}'::jsonb, 'beginner', 'idx_basics', true, '2026-07-14T14:21:14.795502'::timestamptz),
  ('idx-basics-101', 'example', '{"text": "Example: bull vs bear market\n\nYour broker goes bankrupt. Is your stock ownership safe? Explain SIPF''s role.\n\nThis illustrates how bull vs bear market applies in a real Indonesian financial context. Understanding this scenario helps learners recognize similar situations in their own financial decisions.", "source_ids": ["c7c57d03-733f-4fe8-bd15-ce3a1cd4a760", "58e3fb2d-7dbc-4a08-ab1a-379af3fa5c38"]}'::jsonb, 'beginner', 'idx_basics', true, '2026-07-14T14:21:14.795508'::timestamptz),
  ('idx-basics-101', 'example', '{"text": "Example: P/E ratio\n\nBBCA has P/E 18, BBRI has P/E 12. Does this automatically mean BBRI is cheaper?\n\nThis illustrates how P/E ratio applies in a real Indonesian financial context. Understanding this scenario helps learners recognize similar situations in their own financial decisions.", "source_ids": ["c7c57d03-733f-4fe8-bd15-ce3a1cd4a760", "58e3fb2d-7dbc-4a08-ab1a-379af3fa5c38"]}'::jsonb, 'intermediate', 'idx_basics', true, '2026-07-14T14:21:14.795513'::timestamptz),
  ('idx-basics-101', 'example', '{"text": "Example: P/B ratio\n\nCalculate market cap: 20 billion shares outstanding, price Rp 5,000. What is the market cap in trillion?\n\nThis illustrates how P/B ratio applies in a real Indonesian financial context. Understanding this scenario helps learners recognize similar situations in their own financial decisions.", "source_ids": ["c7c57d03-733f-4fe8-bd15-ce3a1cd4a760", "58e3fb2d-7dbc-4a08-ab1a-379af3fa5c38"]}'::jsonb, 'intermediate', 'idx_basics', true, '2026-07-14T14:21:14.795519'::timestamptz),
  ('idx-basics-101', 'example', '{"text": "Example: EPS\n\nThe IDX Composite rises 20% but your stock falls 5%. What are 3 possible explanations?\n\nThis illustrates how EPS applies in a real Indonesian financial context. Understanding this scenario helps learners recognize similar situations in their own financial decisions.", "source_ids": ["c7c57d03-733f-4fe8-bd15-ce3a1cd4a760", "58e3fb2d-7dbc-4a08-ab1a-379af3fa5c38"]}'::jsonb, 'intermediate', 'idx_basics', true, '2026-07-14T14:21:14.795524'::timestamptz),
  ('idx-basics-101', 'example', '{"text": "Example: ROE\n\nCompare investing in IDX30 ETF vs picking 5 individual stocks from LQ45. Pros and cons?\n\nThis illustrates how ROE applies in a real Indonesian financial context. Understanding this scenario helps learners recognize similar situations in their own financial decisions.", "source_ids": ["c7c57d03-733f-4fe8-bd15-ce3a1cd4a760", "58e3fb2d-7dbc-4a08-ab1a-379af3fa5c38"]}'::jsonb, 'intermediate', 'idx_basics', true, '2026-07-14T14:21:14.795529'::timestamptz),
